# Per-path token ceilings, gated by `itok check` (pinned to `--bpe`, so the
# verdict is deterministic). Only registered paths are checked.
#
# WHAT THIS CEILING IS: a cap on ENTRY COST -- what a session loads before any
# work begins. A spec is re-read every turn, so its size is a recurring bill,
# not a one-off. The federation split this repo's law into ten files exactly
# so a session can load one chain (root + hub + node) instead of everything.
#
# It forces a REVIEW, not a shrink. Set with real slack (~12% over measured),
# because a ceiling a hair above current turns every legitimate sentence into
# a raise, and a threshold raised reflexively trains the reflex it exists to
# catch. Raising one is a reviewed decision and belongs in its own commit,
# with the reason.
#
# MEASURED 2026-09-17 with `itok estimate --bpe` (o200k), at the commit that
# wrote this file: 8,548 tokens across ten files. The chain a node actually
# costs is root + hub + that node, which is what `sherd budget` reports.

# The root: goal, constraints, the command surface, the repo gate. Loaded on
# EVERY chain, so it is the one number that is paid ten times over.
#
# RAISED 2000 -> 2280, reviewed. Four things landed at the root since this
# number was set: V44 and T48 (flake inputs pin tags, and the step that
# checks it), and V46 and T51 (the coverage floor and ceiling, and theirs).
# Both are rules WITH runners, which is the pairing this repo requires and
# the reason the root is the file they live in. Compaction ran first: `mth
# archive` folded two finished rows out, worth 45 tokens against the 59
# needed; what is left in §T is open work plus the id-keeping stubs that
# archiving leaves behind. 2280 is ~12% over the new measured 2037.
SPEC.md              2720

# The hub. It owns no logic and should stay this small; if it grows, the
# growth belongs in a node.
src/SPEC.md           420

